hyperplasia, hypothyroidism, central nervous system defects, craniopharyngioma, and Cushing’s disease)
There are a few points in the history that can narrow down the diagnosis. Firstly, this girl has Tanner II breast development indicating that she has been exposed to estrogen;
however, at 16 years age, more developed breasts with higher Tanner stages would be expected.
