oman’s presentation.\n(Option D) DIC is a serious life-threatening condition presenting with low-platelet count, intravascular coagulation, and thrombus formation potentially in every organ system. The\ntwo most common conditions associated with DIC during pregnancy are placental abruption and fetal demise. Laboratory studies show low levels of all of coagulation factors. An\nasymptomatic isolated thrombocytopenia is not a picture consistent with DIC.\n(Option E) Although thrombocytopenia is a common feature of pregnancy-related hypertensive disorders such as pre-eclampsia or HELLP syndrome. With pre-eclampsia other\nmanifestations clinical or laboratory findings would be expected (e.g., proteinuria, hypertension, elevated liver enzymes, headache, abdominal pain, etc.) An isolated mild\nthrombocytopenia in a completely asymptomatic pregnant woman is unlikely to have been caused by pre-eclampsia.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["drug","hypertension","pregnan"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"604395e74d8ae6b53346c0bf4bf81cac91b39300","duplicate_group_id":"exact-604395e74d8a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6a7b5cd430b1e459872c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1017,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_as